#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:5
#: f348cc40286d4870b756bd6c23cc5bc3
msgid "MAVLink2 Signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:7
#: a660e958afd14ee49dfd312d0e3002f3
msgid "ArduPilot and Mission Planner have the ability to add security to over-the-air MAVLink transmissions by adding packet signing using an encrypted key. This does NOT encrypt the data, just merely controls if the autopilot will respond to MAVLink commands or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:9
#: 8c2afb3205a448bb9ce3f99494c98418
msgid "When active in the autopilot, any non-USB serial port can be configured only to respond to MAVLink command requests from Mission Planner if they contain the passkey. This prevents other Ground Control Stations (GCS) that do not know the passkey from reading or writing parameters and sending commands. Something that is possible otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:11
#: d58d6bc9f91e42e99d0b09b152c2d85f
msgid "Telemetry downlink data is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:13
#: 2fa3d862ec6d4249a84065657e602d0d
msgid "USB connections are unaffected, allowing full connection to an autopilot using an unknown passkey and allowing the user to erase (disable signing) or change the passkey it uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:16
#: bda7b852e7bf4ce1b69642212810ba68
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:18
#: e16587a6650e476c88da97619e64a2f5
msgid "Make sure the telemetry port protocol is set to option = 2 (MAVLink2). Communication with any serial port using MAVLink 1 is not protected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:20
#: 011f81e1808748fe8df5433fc49d187e
msgid "In Mission Planner, connect the autopilot, use the SETUP menu  and the Advanced submenu, and press \"Mavlink Signing\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:25
#: ebc86002b88b410e9641ac50f6abc382
msgid "The dialog will show a list of all the passkeys already setup for Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:27
#: 3106ef72c7634267b5837cc0e0c46e77
msgid "This dialog can be used to create new keys using the ``ADD`` button.A key may be removed from the list by selecting and pressing delete on the PC and then the ``SAVE`` button5350. You can also do this while unconnected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:29
#: b3f4abd5fb6949f78f31634c296538c0
msgid "To setup the autopilot to use a key from the list, press the ``USE`` button on a key while connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:31
#: f57e8aedc96e4fa4900b959ffcac79e1
msgid "You can check if the link is now signing by clicking \"Stats...\" under the comm port drop down box used for selecting which port to connect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:33
#: 5c74af4c0c6f4d989e1234b109938920
msgid "To remove and disable signing for a connected autopilot, press the ``Disable Signing`` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:36
#: 1aaa4689535d46d2b3fa73be96a3e430
msgid "Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:38
#: cad9378bc64f4d0fa4491e3ae9507e68
msgid "Once the autopilot is using signing, USB connections are unaffected, but any link via a SERIAL port using MAVLink2 protocol will only respond to MAVLink commands if they are signed with the key the autopilot is using. But links will still receive telemetry updates even if they are not using signing with the active key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MAVLink2-signing.rst:40
#: bf462e5b694c46d193fe73c8ae8e7c1b
msgid "When you connect Mission Planner over a link that is signing, it will see if it has the correct key stored in its keys table that you would have setup previously. If it does, the connection will use that key and commands will be acted upon by the autopilot, including parameter download at connection. If you connect, but parameter download does not occur, then the key was not present. Add the key, and re-connect."
msgstr ""
